## Conversation
Second P2 from dmitry-tokarev-nv on PR #14965: every router recorded one provenance entry per cached block per worker even with `--shared-cache-type none`, because the ZMQ decoder reads an absent `shared_cache_eligible` as eligible and no Python producer sends the key. Reviewer asked to gate the map on the configured shared-cache type.

## Actions
Used an explore subagent to trace SharedCacheType -> Indexer -> RadixTree. Finding: RadixTree is built inside KvIndexer::from_builder with only KvIndexerBuilder in scope; the shared-cache observer lives on the `Indexer` enum, not the tree; the only consumer of dump provenance is `restore_dump_provenance` on the dump/replay path (worker TreeDump -> router try_apply_event -> observer.observe_stored). Changed `shared_cache_provenance` to `Option<...>` (None = off), added `RadixTree::enable_shared_cache_provenance`, `KvIndexerBuilder::shared_cache_provenance(bool)`, gated the two frontend `Indexer::Single` sites on `shared_cache_type != None`, and made LocalKvIndexer always enable it. Added a default-off regression test; two existing provenance tests opt in via a helper. Ran full `cargo test -p dynamo-kv-router` (1073 pass).

## Errors & Mistakes
None.

## Dead Ends
Considered storing eligibility inside NodeState instead of a side map; rejected as a larger redesign touching CRTC. Considered plumbing a Mooncake flag from Python into KvEventPublisher/KvStateAgent so the worker side could gate too; rejected as out of scope for the review item, and the worker map only holds its own blocks.

## Hints for Future Agents
- The worker-side LocalKvIndexer (publisher/mod.rs, state_agent.rs) has no KvRouterConfig, so it cannot gate on router config. If it is ever gated off, TreeDump recovery will hand a mooncake-store router all-false eligibility and it will forget learned edges on recovery.
- The concurrent trees (ConcurrentRadixTree, CRTC) have no provenance map and dump `shared_cache_eligible: false`; frontends with router_event_threads > 1 already lose provenance on dump.
- `KvIndexer::new_with_pruning` / `new_with_approximate_retention` are still used by bench, mocker, remote side indexer, and backend.rs; do not remove them.
- The Python `RadixTree` binding (lib/bindings/python/rust/llm/kv.rs) calls `RadixTree::new()` and now dumps without provenance; no Python test depends on it.

## Codebase Discoveries
lib/kvbm-consolidator/src/wire/router_out.rs emits BlockStored with `medium: None` and no `shared_cache_eligible`, so consolidator events arrive as eligible primary stores. Not reachable for the Mooncake cache because `observe_stored` also requires the source in `allowed_sources`, which needs a published Mooncake contract.

